<title>USA: Consumers 780 MW Mich. nuke boosting power.</title>
<headline>Consumers 780 MW Mich. nuke boosting power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Energy's 780 megawatt Palisades nuclear power plant was operating at 57 percent of capacity and boosting power as of early Wednesday, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>The plant, located in South Haven, Mich., was being ramped up to full power from a repair shutdown which began last week.</p>
<p>Palisades produces 18 percent of Consumers Energy's total electrical output.</p>
<p>Consumers Energy is a subsidiary of CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
</text>
